00:03:56.950 --> 00:04:00.840
The enemy will have noticed us by now. Stay alert.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:05.260
<i>I know! You're starting to sound like Rey! It's throwing me off!</i>

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:10.770
<b>Stardust Battlefield</b>

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:10.770
<b>Stardust Battlefield</b>

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:11.230
Changes to the enemy ship?

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:13.900
No, sir! Course and speed are the same!

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:19.220
Okay, load launcher one to launcher six, numbers one through four with Dispars!

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:23.120
Activate CIWS and Tristans! We'll get them this time!

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:24.580
Mr. Chairman! That's...

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:58.480
Do not worry, Representative Athha.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:02.440
I'm not challenging him for his actions.

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:05.680
I understand what happened,

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:10.540
as well as the measures taken against him and others by former Chairwoman Canaver.

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:16.170
It's just that, if I were to talk to you, I'd rather talk to the real you,

00:05:17.140 --> 00:05:18.100
Athrun.

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:20.560
That's all.

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:30.100
<i>Why? Why isn't anything happening yet?</i>

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:33.270
Impulse, 1400 from Bogey One.

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:35.480
Hasn't it changed its course yet?

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:38.500
What's going on? Is this part of a plan?

00:05:39.140 --> 00:05:39.860
Shit!

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:40.820
It's a decoy!

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:47.240
Okay, let's do it!

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:48.260
Okay.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:59.460
Shawn!

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:03.880
Scatter and fight them separately!

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:08.160
Damn! They were waiting for us!

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:11.260
Bogey One?!

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:13.430
We've lost Bogey One!

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:14.290
What?!

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:17.770
Shawn's machine isn't responding!

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:21.190
Three heat sources at Yellow 62, Beta.

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:25.180
It's them... Chaos, Gaia and Abyss!

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:28.070
Find me that enemy vessel, Bogey One, now!

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:32.410
Send out the Dagger Team! Start the engines!

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:37.580
Fire missile launchers five through eight! Aim main cannon at enemy battleship!

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:50.050
Heat source at Blue 18, Mark 9, Charlie!

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:52.720
It's Bogey One! Distance 500!

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:53.830
What?!

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:55.140
Also, two mobile suits!

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:56.540
Behind us?

00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:58.560
Detecting targeting lasers, directed at us!

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:06.320
Fire anti-beam depth charges! Thirty to starboard! Aim Tristans now!

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:09.740
Can't do it! Mobile suits at Orange 22, Delta!

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:14.080
Engines to maximum! Turn us around using that starboard asteroid as a shield!

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:30.720
Meyrin! Bring Shinn and the others back!

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:33.060
And prepare to send out our remaining machines!

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:33.660
Yes, ma'am!

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:34.260
Malik!

00:07:34.530 --> 00:07:38.180
Use the asteroid's surface features to protect us from any direct hits!

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:39.160
Yes, ma'am!

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:41.270
Arthur! Counterattack!

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:44.800
Launcher five! Launcher ten! Dispars! Fire!

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:52.820
You're mine!

00:07:58.300 --> 00:07:59.540
<i>Dale!</i>

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:05.600
<i>We're already down by two!</i>

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:12.170
<i>The Minerva's... You mean, we walked right into their trap?</i>

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:17.140
Yeah, it looks that way. But there's no way we can get back right now!

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:24.600
Neidhardts, fire!

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:31.280
With them on our tail, there's nothing we can do!

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:33.080
Can't we get behind them?!

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:35.410
No, ma'am! We've got our hands full just evading.

00:08:35.670 --> 00:08:36.800
Send out Rey's ZAKU!

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:38.900
We can't get a clear course to send anyone out!

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:01.310
Who do you think you are?!

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:05.390
You thieves!

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:08.230
You're going down.

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:19.890
Get behind him, Auel. We'll take his head!

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:22.540
I don't really want it, but okay.

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:26.870
I can't get their position.

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:27.880
<i>Shinn!</i>

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:38.010
What is it with you?!

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:48.060
Half of our firepower is useless here!

00:09:48.390 --> 00:09:51.940
Drifting rocks are getting in the way! Our shots aren't reaching the enemy!

00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:54.770
A tough nut to crack.

00:09:54.770 --> 00:09:57.820
We win if they stop moving.

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:01.950
Blow that asteroid they're clinging to up!

00:10:02.340 --> 00:10:05.410
Let's see how they enjoy a shower of debris!

00:10:05.770 --> 00:10:07.560
I want their hull to be buried in it!

00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:08.330
Yes, sir!

00:10:08.980 --> 00:10:11.950
I'm going out to finish them off. Take over for me.

00:10:11.950 --> 00:10:12.460
Yes, sir.

00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:15.130
Missiles approaching! Six of them!

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:16.760
Counterattack!

00:10:17.030 --> 00:10:18.430
But these missiles...

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:20.480
<i>They're not aiming at us.</i>

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:26.520
Look out! Get the ship away from the asteroid!

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:37.280
Our starboard... Captain!

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:40.240
Get us out of here! Raise bow by fifteen!

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:44.620
Second wave of missiles approaching!

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:46.000
Decelerate twenty!

00:10:57.010 --> 00:11:02.050
Now... I'm really sorry to do this before your launching ceremony,

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:05.140
but this is where your voyage ends!

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:12.020
Thrusters number four and six damaged.

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:14.190
Captain! We're getting trapped!

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:18.820
Our route is being closed off!

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:21.240
Mobile armor and mobile suits approaching!

00:11:25.790 --> 00:11:27.790
Aves, send out Rey!

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:30.460
<i>Ma'am! Our catapult isn't</i>—

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:33.690
Walk him out if you have to! Hurry!

00:11:33.690 --> 00:11:34.380
{split}Where are Shinn and the others?!

00:11:34.940 --> 00:11:38.510
The Impulse and ZAKU are still in a battle against Chaos, Gaia, and Abyss!

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:41.680
Aren't there any more mobile suits on this ship?!

00:11:42.340 --> 00:11:43.840
We have no pilots!

00:11:46.280 --> 00:11:49.220
Captain! We can crush the cliff ahead of us with the Tannhauser...

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:54.200
That'll only scatter rock toward us as we approach the next layer of solid rock!

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:55.560
R-Right...

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:13.710
<i>Gil's aboard the Minerva! I won't allow you to sink it!</i>

00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:19.550
Damn! The Minerva's...

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:21.710
It'll sink unless we hurry back!

00:12:21.710 --> 00:12:22.590
I know that!

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:33.480
What?!

00:12:36.260 --> 00:12:38.570
How many starboard thrusters are still functioning?!

00:12:42.540 --> 00:12:48.310
Six. But we'll be target practice for them if we head out there now!

00:12:48.310 --> 00:12:52.410
Fire everything on starboard all at once, against the asteroid!

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:55.000
What?!

00:12:55.410 --> 00:12:58.470
We'll push the hull out in one motion with the force of the explosion

00:12:58.470 --> 00:12:59.920
together with the rocks surrounding us.

00:13:01.790 --> 00:13:05.430
Don't be ridiculous! Think of the damage to the Minerva's hull if we did that!

00:13:05.740 --> 00:13:08.220
Right now the priority is to get out of here.

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:11.350
We're nothing but a target if we stay here.

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:16.520
Talia.

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:19.320
You have a point.

00:13:20.100 --> 00:13:21.940
Okay, let's give it a try.

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:22.900
Captain!

00:13:23.540 --> 00:13:25.940
We'll talk about this later, Arthur.

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:29.070
Prepare to fire all starboard weapons!

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:33.870
Starboard thrusters to maximum as we fire! Match the timing!

00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:36.290
Preparing to fire all starboard weapons.

00:13:36.740 --> 00:13:39.250
Engaging starboard thrusters on signal!

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:49.800
What is it with you, White Baldy?!

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:55.100
Outta my way!

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:00.180
<i>Jon!</i>

00:14:00.180 --> 00:14:02.780
Get back, Miller! He's out of your league!

00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:04.670
<i>Return and guard the ship!</i>

00:14:04.670 --> 00:14:05.610
Yes, sir!

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:09.160
I won't let you!

00:14:09.840 --> 00:14:10.780
Not so easy!

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:55.990
That guy. That guy!

00:15:02.360 --> 00:15:06.420
Damn! Why can't I hit him?! It's the same as last time!

00:15:07.450 --> 00:15:09.090
Now, for the finish.

00:15:09.820 --> 00:15:12.760
We can't count on a direct hit. There are too many rocks in the way.

00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:15.810
Just corner them so they can't come after us.

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:17.930
The Captain might not be satisfied

00:15:18.510 --> 00:15:22.600
but our mobile suits are running out of power.

00:15:22.910 --> 00:15:25.270
Bogey One, distance 150.

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:28.740
All hands, brace for impact! Here we go!

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:33.780
Starboard thrusters to maximum!

00:15:36.440 --> 00:15:38.580
All starboard cannons, fire!!

00:15:58.240 --> 00:15:59.060
The Minerva!

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:03.600
Turn bow thirty! Fire at Bogey One!

00:16:03.930 --> 00:16:06.580
Aiming Tannhauser! Bogey One!

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:13.110
Evade! Hard to port!

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:14.030
Fire!

00:16:32.070 --> 00:16:34.970
They've risen from the brink of defeat!

00:16:48.260 --> 00:16:51.990
Send the retreat signal to Oakley and the others! We're leaving this area!

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:57.820
I look forward to seeing you again,

00:16:58.340 --> 00:17:01.820
White Baldy, and the rest of the ZAFT crew.

00:17:15.580 --> 00:17:18.010
<i>Damn. Game over with only two kills.</i>

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:21.470
Whatever. Stella, Neo's calling.

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:23.120
<i>He says to come back.</i>

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:36.230
Bogey One is leaving.

00:17:36.230 --> 00:17:39.700
Power has reached critical level on both the Impulse and Lunamaria's ZAKU.

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:44.660
Captain. With that explosion our number two engine and portside heat sensors have also been damaged!

00:17:44.970 --> 00:17:46.180
Captain Gladys.

00:17:47.400 --> 00:17:50.540
You've done enough. We'll think of another plan.

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:57.130
I personally cannot inconvenience Representative Athha any longer.

00:17:58.160 --> 00:17:59.640
I'm very sorry.

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:16.140
I sincerely apologize for everything, Representative Athha.

00:18:16.140 --> 00:18:17.900
Never mind us.

00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:22.640
Although, I must say I very much regret that things ended this way.

00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:26.360
I pray from my heart that you're able to resolve things quickly.

00:18:26.360 --> 00:18:27.750
Thank you very much.

00:18:32.240 --> 00:18:34.590
Shinn! Lunamaria! Rey!

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:38.050
You must be exhausted. Are you all right?

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:41.220
We've finally reestablished contact with the homeland.

00:18:43.960 --> 00:18:46.420
Athrun Zala? Him?

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:52.800
I'm told that rescue teams and investigation units are on their way to Armory One,

00:18:52.800 --> 00:18:57.780
so I've requested that they send a vessel our way to pick you up.

00:18:58.060 --> 00:18:58.980
Thank you.

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:04.940
But really, this young man saved us earlier, didn't he, Captain?

00:19:04.940 --> 00:19:07.160
Ah... Yes...

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:10.620
That was most impressive.

00:19:11.130 --> 00:19:14.500
The true strength of someone who has survived numerous battles.

00:19:14.870 --> 00:19:19.970
Thank you. But I apologize for sticking my nose into things like I did.

00:19:21.340 --> 00:19:24.500
Your decision was the correct one. Thank you.

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:28.800
Excuse me!

00:19:33.160 --> 00:19:36.020
<i>Aren't there any more mobile suits on this ship?!</i>

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:38.500
<i>We have no pilots!</i>

00:19:38.500 --> 00:19:40.740
<i>Shawn's machine isn't responding!</i>

00:19:57.210 --> 00:19:59.760
<i>Then what if that name is not real?</i>

00:20:02.060 --> 00:20:06.020
<i>Would that mean its existence is not real either?</i>

00:20:06.020 --> 00:20:08.220
<i>Is that what it would mean?</i>

00:20:11.360 --> 00:20:15.520
Did he really have to change his name, though?

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:17.620
Think of what he was before.

00:20:17.620 --> 00:20:19.720
Are you serious?

00:20:19.720 --> 00:20:21.060
Regardless of his past...

00:20:27.920 --> 00:20:32.820
Well... We were just talking about you, Athrun Zala.

00:20:34.320 --> 00:20:37.500
Hard to believe, but it figures.

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:41.620
I'm honored to have the chance to meet such a legendary ace in the least expected of places.

00:20:42.780 --> 00:20:46.510
I'm not anything like that. I'm just Alex.

00:20:47.620 --> 00:20:50.430
So you no longer have to pilot a mobile suit?

00:20:51.890 --> 00:20:55.500
Stop it, Luna! Who cares about anyone living in Orb?

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:57.060
They have no idea about what really goes on.

00:20:59.760 --> 00:21:00.920
Excuse me.

00:21:02.580 --> 00:21:05.910
But I hear you saved this ship.

00:21:06.440 --> 00:21:08.020
For that, I thank you.

00:21:09.560 --> 00:21:12.000
Hey, wait for me! Hey, Sis!

00:21:18.450 --> 00:21:20.140
That can't be possible.

00:21:20.140 --> 00:21:22.090
No, I've checked it multiple times.

00:21:22.410 --> 00:21:24.520
Look here. This one's from two hours ago.

00:21:25.160 --> 00:21:27.760
Although it's very gradual, even now it's unmistakably moving.

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:32.080
That's impossible! Junius Seven should be in a fixed orbit.

00:22:08.680 --> 00:22:10.100
<i>Hi! Mayu here!</i>

00:22:10.630 --> 00:22:14.020
<i>I'm sorry. I can't talk to you right now!</i>

00:22:14.590 --> 00:22:18.310
<i>I'll call you back later, so please leave your name after the beep!</i>

00:22:18.310 --> 00:22:25.740
<b>kotoba wo kasanete mo wakari aenai koto</b>

00:22:18.310 --> 00:22:25.740
I still did not realize

00:22:25.030 --> 00:22:32.530
<b>
mada shiranakatta ne</b>

00:22:25.030 --> 00:22:32.530
That there are things that can't be conveyed even with words

00:22:31.830 --> 00:22:40.170
<b>kimi dake wo dakishimetakute nakushita yume kimi wa</b>

00:22:31.830 --> 00:22:40.170
My lost dreams of wanting to hold you by my side,

00:22:39.500 --> 00:22:47.130
<b>
"akiramenaide" to itta</b>

00:22:39.500 --> 00:22:47.130
For them, you said, "Don't give up!"

00:22:46.420 --> 00:22:53.970
<b>tooku hanareteru hodo ni chikaku ni kanjiteru</b>

00:22:46.420 --> 00:22:53.970
The further we are apart, the nearer I feel you are

00:22:53.260 --> 00:23:02.110
<b>
samishisa mo tsuyosa eto kawatteku... kimi wo omottanara</b>

00:22:53.260 --> 00:23:02.110
Even my loneliness turns into strength... when I think of you

00:23:01.440 --> 00:23:08.820
<b>setsunaku mune wo sasu sore wa yume no kakera</b>

00:23:01.440 --> 00:23:08.820
The thing that pierces the gentle chest, that's a fragment of my dream

00:23:08.110 --> 00:23:21.790
<b>
arinomama deaeteta sono kiseki mou ichido shinjite</b>

00:23:08.110 --> 00:23:21.790
Believe once more in the the miracle that is our chanced meeting

00:23:21.960 --> 00:23:23.920
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:21.960 --> 00:23:23.920
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:23.920 --> 00:23:25.340
The tombstone has begun to move.

00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:29.670
Is it the memories of the loved ones who perished that freezes over,

00:23:30.700 --> 00:23:33.180
or is it the tears of those who have lost loved ones?

00:23:35.430 --> 00:23:39.640
The voices of sorrow once again pierce Athrun's heart.

00:23:40.790 --> 00:23:44.480
Next, on Mobile Suit Gundam Seed Destiny,

00:23:44.480 --> 00:23:45.650
"Scars that Won't Heal."

00:23:45.940 --> 00:23:51.950
<b>Next time</b>

00:23:45.940 --> 00:23:51.950
<b>Next time</b>

00:23:45.940 --> 00:23:51.950
<b>Scars That Won't Heal</b>

00:23:45.940 --> 00:23:51.950
<b>Scars That Won't Heal</b>

00:23:46.660 --> 00:23:49.380
Reveal your earnest thoughts, GINN!
